==================================================
BACKGROUND — PHASE 3J FINDINGS
==================================================

Phase 3J audited 36,494 historical attacking observations across
2022/23–2025/26.

Phase 3H successfully corrected the extreme cross-position distortion,
but Phase 3J identified a second calibration problem.

Phase 3H applied the following xG/xA calibration only to £10m+ players:

prem_xg_ratio = 1.882x
prem_xa_ratio = 3.020x

Players below £10m instead received:

non_prem_xg_ratio = 0.984x
non_prem_xa_ratio = 1.446x

This creates an artificial binary threshold.

Historical Phase 3J results:

£12m+:
Predicted calibrated xP = 5.40
Actual FPL points = 5.74
Bias = +0.34

£10m–£12m:
Predicted calibrated xP = 3.67
Actual = 4.29
Bias = +0.62

£8m–£10m:
Predicted calibrated xP = 2.39
Actual = 3.62
Bias = +1.23

£6m–£8m:
Predicted calibrated xP = 1.93
Actual = 2.81
Bias = +0.88

Therefore:

£10m+ calibration is broadly successful.

£8m–£10m attackers remain systematically underpredicted.

£6m–£8m attackers remain systematically underpredicted.

==================================================
ROLE FINDING
==================================================

Phase 3J also established that FPL position alone is insufficient.

Historical attacking archetypes:

Elite Striker:
9.18 pts/90

Inside Forward / Goalscoring Winger:
8.53 pts/90

Creative Winger / Playmaker:
7.50 pts/90

Central / Box-to-Box Midfielder:
7.60 pts/90

The current MID/FWD distinction hides meaningful attacking-role
differences.

Phase 3J therefore recommended:

1. Piecewise price-tier calibration
2. Role-aware calibration
3. Retaining underlying football data rather than raw historical
   FPL points

